TRPG Project — Renderer World/Native Pass Split (Session Summary)
What we did this session

Diagnosed: blurry text after resolution change, caused by SDL's letterbox logical-presentation stretching a fixed-resolution canvas up to the real window size (linear filtering), unrelated to font size or DPI.

Root fix implemented and confirmed compiling/working in-game:

Renderer now owns its own SDL_Texture* m_logicalTarget (SDL_TEXTUREACCESS_TARGET, created in setLogicalPresentation()) instead of using SDL_SetRenderLogicalPresentation. This replaces SDL's automatic logical-presentation scaling with manual control.
New beginWorldPass() / endWorldPass(): the former targets the internal texture and clears it; the latter switches back to the window, computes a manual letterbox rect (computeLetterboxTransform() — same uniform-scale-fit math SDL's own letterbox used), and stretches the texture into it with a controllable ScaleMode via setLogicalScaleMode().
New "native/UI" default mode: when not inside a world pass, every primitive (fillRect, drawRect, drawLine, renderText, drawTexture) transparently converts logical coordinates to physical window pixels via toNativeRect()/toNativePos() — same scale+offset math as the letterbox. No UI window file needs to change — they keep passing logical coordinates (Rectf{0,0,VIEW_W,24}) as before.
The actual crispness fix: renderText() now temporarily bumps the font's point size via TTF_SetFontSize() (new ScopedFontSize RAII guard, same pattern as the existing ScopedFontStyle) before rasterizing, scaled by the native-pass scale factor — so glyphs are rasterized at real on-screen pixel density, not just repositioned/stretched as a small bitmap. Text's resulting texture is drawn 1:1 (no size scaling), only its position goes through the native transform — this asymmetry (position scaled, size not) is intentional and was flagged explicitly to avoid double-scaling.
measureText() deliberately untouched — still reports logical-space sizes, so all existing UI layout math (everything built this session in SettingsRowWindow, ConfirmWindow, etc.) stays correct with zero changes.
Added proper Rule-of-5 to Renderer (previously default-constructible/copyable with no real resources) since it now owns an SDL texture — move-only, copy deleted.
Verified no conflict with UIScale: UIScale::factor() (clamped [0.75, 1.0], shrinks logical-space sizes for small windows) and the new native-pass transform (converts already-decided logical coordinates to physical pixels) solve different problems and compose correctly — confirmed by reading UIScale.cpp, no changes needed there.
Verified DamagePreview draws in fixed screen coordinates (not camera-relative) → belongs in native pass.
Verified CombatAnimationSystem::render() is currently an empty no-op stub → correctly stays categorized for the future world pass (per its own TODO), no action needed now.
